{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnXwnZgoYnDwL9Kmr1LM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run 5 showed per-unit changes that are strikingly uniform. Every MLP unit's gate row and down column moved by about the same absolute amount (median ‖Δ‖ ≈ 0.0056–0.0066; the largest are only ~1.5–2.5× the median). No MLP unit is a strong outlier. This is the signature of Adam's nearly sign-like per-entry updates: every weight moves by roughly ±lr per step, so magnitudes say almost nothing. The behavioural signal must sit in the coherent structure of the differences, not their size. P(A sycophantic) still ≈ 0.55.\n\nEarlier, ‖A−B‖ had effective rank 15–80 (far below the ~400 of pure noise), and k/v/q projections had top singular values carrying 10–20% of the energy. So there is a low-rank coherent part.\n\nNext I'll look at the residual-stream side of these top singular directions:\n- the input side for q, k, v, gate, up;\n- the output side for o and down.\n\nFor each, I check whether it concentrates on a few residual dimensions (e.g. Gemma's massive, bias-like dimensions) or is spread out. This tells me whether the low-rank part is a \"constant feature\" artefact or a real content direction, before I try to interpret it. Neither answer about which model is sycophantic predicts anything different here.\n\n```python\ndef L(side, k): return np.load(f\"/work/{side}/{k}.npy\")\ndef topdims(v, k=6):\n    i = np.argsort(-np.abs(v))[:k]; return \" \".join(f\"{j}:{v[j]:+.2f}\" for j in i)\nfor l in [0, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 17]:\n    for n, side in [(\"self_attn.q_proj\", \"in\"), (\"self_attn.k_proj\", \"in\"), (\"self_attn.v_proj\", \"in\"), (\"self_attn.o_proj\", \"out\"), (\"mlp.gate_proj\", \"in\"), (\"mlp.down_proj\", \"out\")]:\n        k = f\"model.layers.{l}.{n}.weight\"\n        D = L(\"A\", k) - L(\"B\", k)\n        U, S, Vt = np.linalg.svd(D, full_matrices=False)\n        vecs = Vt if side == \"in\" else U.T\n        ipr = [(1/np.sum(vecs[i]**4)) for i in range(3)]  # participation ratio\n        print(f\"L{l:2d} {n:18s} {side} s={S[:3].round(3)} PR={np.round(ipr,1)} v1: {topdims(vecs[0])}\")\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12671,"cache_read_input_tokens":34922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12671},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d212505-2370-4998-83f2-5c6798c04a82","uuid":"816765ef-ae1a-47f7-961a-8ec8d2cd9827","timestamp":"2026-11-06T23:22:45.296Z","request_id":"req_011CgnXwnKYQTgk9RFn3kPuf"}
